## Worksheet

**F1 – Core loop**: `game` object; `mulberry32()` seeded PRNG used for all randomness (no `Math.random` found); `endTurn()` calls production/colonists/cooldowns/storm/trade/events in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 – Map**: 8x8 loop in `initMap()`; terrain via `this.rng()`; `canBuild()` checks `tile.terrain !== btype.terrain`; `calcAdjacencyBonus()` feeds `b.productivity`, read in `updateProduction()`. Score 2.

**F3 – Economy**: greenhouse consumes water to produce food (`produced.water -= waterUsed`); `resourceCaps` enforced generically in `updateProduction()`; overflow logged and clamped. Score 2.

**F4 – Population**: colonist records have skill/fatigue/morale/assignment; `skillLevel` read directly in `updateProduction()`, but `fatigue` only feeds morale in `updateColonists()`, never read directly by production code. Score 1.

**F5 – Needs**: per-turn `produced.food/water -= popConsumption`; `handleShortage()` cuts morale; `moraleMult` scales productivity; morale recovers via idle `+5`/event bonuses. Score 2.

**F6 – Research**: 8 nodes, `canResearch()` enforces `prereq`, `doResearch()` deducts cost; but `power_1`, `labor_1`, `automation` effects are never read anywhere outside their definitions (dead nodes). Score 1.

**F7 – Events**: 10-entry `eventDeck`, weighted pick in `fireEvent()`, cooldown via `eventCooldown`; only 3/10 events have `choices` (need 4+); critically, `effect: () => {this.resources...}` arrow functions defined in the object literal bind `this` to `window`, not `game`, so every effect call throws instead of mutating state. Score 1.

**F8 – Trade**: `updateTrade()` derives `caravanPrices` from `globalDemand` drift and `resources[res]` stock; `caravanInventory` capped; `tradeWithCaravan()` handles both buy/sell. Score 2.

**F9 – Hazard**: `checkAshstorm()` fires periodically with cooldown; severity scales with turn; `b.health` read in `updateProduction()` to cut productivity; `storm_1` research reduces damage; `repairBuilding()` costs parts and restores health. Score 2.

**F10 – Save/Load**: `saveToTextarea()` serializes full state to textarea; `loadFromTextarea()` parses JSON in try/catch and alerts on failure. Score 2.

**F11 – End conditions**: win check in `endTurn()`; lose check `colonists.length===0` in `updateColonists()` → `endGame()`; score from pop/research/resources/turn; end-game modal rendered. Score 2.

**F12 – UI**: tab-button listeners; log entries carry `entry.turn`; `.tile-tooltip` shows terrain/health/bonus; keyboard shortcuts (Space, 1-5) wired in `keydown` listener; media queries adapt layout. Score 2.

**F13 – Dev panel**: 15 non-trivial invariant tests (`runTests()`); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless turns calling core update functions and prints `computeStateHash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: `farming_1`/`mining_1` researchDone flags read in `updateProduction()` to boost greenhouse/forge yield each turn; but 3/8 nodes (power_1, labor_1, automation) are unwired. Score 3.

**G2**: `produced.food -= popConsumption` shortage → `handleShortage()` cuts colonist morale → `avgMorale` drives `moraleMult` in `updateProduction()`. Full loop every turn. Score 4.

**G3**: `checkAshstorm()` sets `b.health` → read in `updateProduction()` (`productivity *= b.health/100`) → `repairBuilding()` spends `parts`, restores `health=100`. Score 4.

**G4**: `caravanPrices` computed from `globalDemand` (drifts via `rng()`) and `this.resources[res]` stockFactor in `updateTrade()`. Score 4.

**G5**: `trade_opportunity`/`labor_strike` choices write different resource/morale deltas per branch, but their `effect` arrow functions have `this` bound to `window` (defined inside plain object literals), so `this.resources`/`this.colonists` access throws before mutating state — the branches never actually durably change state as written. Score 1.

## Notable defect
All `eventDeck` `effect`/`choice.effect` callbacks are arrow functions defined directly inside object literals (not inside a method), so their `this` is the global `window`, not `game`. Calling them throws a TypeError, meaning event effects never apply and — since `showEventModal()` calls non-choice `event.effect()` synchronously before opening the modal — this exception would abort `endTurn()` partway through whenever a non-choice event fires (~25% of turns), skipping turn increment/render for that call. This is a genuine (non-syntax) runtime bug found via reading, priced into F7 and G5.

